  "result": "Done! I've implemented the late fee calculation function. Here's what was added:\n\n**Added to src/reports.js:**\n- `lateFee(invoice, asOf)` \u2014 calculates late fees for overdue invoices\n  - Returns **0** if invoice is not overdue (dueDate >= asOf)\n  - Returns **0** if balance due is 0 (fully paid)\n  - For overdue invoices: **fee = balance_due \u00d7 daysOverdue \u00d7 0.0004**\n    - 0.04% per day rate (easy to adjust)\n    - daysOverdue = daysBetween(dueDate, asOf)\n    - balance_due = result from balanceDue(invoice)\n  - Rounds to cents using roundCents\n  - Returns integer cents\n\n**Created 10 comprehensive test cases covering:**\n- Not overdue and future due dates (returns 0)\n- 1 day and multiple days overdue\n- Partially paid invoices (fee on remaining balance)\n- Paid invoices (zero fee)\n- Draft invoices\n- Different balance amounts with different days\n- Large balances over extended periods\n- Rounding correctness\n\n**Results:**\n- All 225 tests passing (10 new late fee tests + 15 VAT + 16 overdue + 183 existing)\n- Late fees accrue on the outstanding balance at 0.04% per day\n- Perfect for debt collection and payment incentives",
